<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices rise at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices rise at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills rose at Monday's primary auction on total demand of 2.289 billion zlotys against a 1.3 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold the entire 1.3 billion offer.</p>
<p>    T-bill	     13-week    26-week    52-week</p>
<p>  new min price    94.97	90.22	82.18</p>
<p>  (pvs auction)   (94.91)    (90.20)    (82.14)</p>
<p>  new max price    95.05	90.43	82.34</p>
<p>  (pvs auction)   (95.03)    (94.95)    (82.50)</p>
<p>  offer		400.0	300.0	600.0</p>
<p>  bids recorded    748.0	380.9     1160.4</p>
<p>  bids accepted    400.0	300.0	600.0</p>
<p>  next auction     300.0	300.0	600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
